  question: 'How Do the Warranty and Maintenance Work Together?',
  answer: [
    'Every Appalachian Sheds building includes the 30-Year Structural Warranty, which covers qualifying structural defects in covered work under its written terms and requires the exterior to be painted within 30 days of completion (vinyl-sided buildings are exempt). It does not replace homeowner maintenance, site drainage, exterior finish care, normal wear or responsible use.',
    'The safest approach: read the warranty, keep water and vegetation away from the lower walls, keep up any paint, stain and caulk, maintain doors and windows, watch roof runoff and document concerns early.',
    'A strong warranty is valuable, but the best protection is a building that is built well, maintained consistently and used as designed.',
